  "orthography_note": "Names are written exactly as the source spells them. The source prints level-1 names in ALL CAPS; they were down-cased with an Azerbaijani-aware mapping in which I→ı and İ→i. A default toLowerCase()/.lower() corrupts both. The Bakı rayon names were taken verbatim in their source mixed case and never re-cased.",
  "naxcivan_note": "NAXÇIVAN MUXTAR RESPUBLİKASI (10000000) carries status digit 0: it is a grouping header, not an administrative unit, and is NOT emitted. Its 7 rayons carry status digit 1 and are PEERS of mainland rayons, not nested one level deeper, so their `parent` is null. The `in_naxcivan_ar` flag is a DISPLAY grouping hint only (derived from code prefix '1'); it is not a hierarchy level.",
  "warnings": [
    {
      "id": "lankaran_saki_yevlax_rayon_divergence",
      "severity": "product_decision",
      "affects": [
        "Lənkəran",
        "Şəki",
        "Yevlax"
      ],
      "detail": "The 2024 classification has NO separate rayon entry for these three: the city entry absorbs the surrounding rural territory. Verified directly — the candidate rayon codes 80200001, 40400001 and 90100001 do not occur anywhere in the document, while Lənkəran şəhəri carries 83 villages, Şəki şəhəri 68 and Yevlax şəhəri 46. BUT the same agency's population workbook (001_16.xls) contains data rows literally spelled 'Lənkəran rayonu' and 'Yevlax rayonu'. Both spellings are officially attested. A parent in rural Lənkəran will look for 'Lənkəran rayonu' and not find it. This file emits ONLY the classification's form (republic_city). Whether to also surface a '<name> rayonu' alias is an OWNER DECISION, not a data gap — it is flagged here, not resolved.",
      "note_xankandi": "Xankəndi is often grouped with these three but does NOT share the divergence: its count block shows zero villages absorbed, so there is no rural population looking for a 'Xankəndi rayonu'."
    },
    {
      "id": "existing_15_mix_categories",
      "severity": "import_blocker",
      "detail": "The platform's existing 15 `districts` rows mix categories and will not extend cleanly. Quba, Şamaxı, Qəbələ, Gədəbəy and Ağdam are RAYONS, not cities. Xırdalan is neither — it is a rayon-subordinate city inside Abşeron rayonu. Naftalan and Xankəndi are absent from the platform entirely. See `existing_platform_mapping` for the row-by-row mapping the import must honour so that no existing row is duplicated or orphaned.",
      "table_naming": "The `districts` table holds CITIES while `city_districts` holds intra-city rayons. Loading 64 country-level rayons into `districts` would make that table name mean three different things. Worth resolving before the import, not after."
    }
  ],
